426 0 obj
<</E(Leave of Absence for mental health reasons is granted on condition that the student�s capacity to resume studies should be assessed upon applying to return to the University. This is to ensure that optimal conditions for the student�s successful reintegra\
tion into the University can be established.)/K[2]/Pg 30 0 R/S/H2/T(Leave of Absence for mental health reasons is granted on condition that the student�s capacity to resume studies should be assessed upon applying to return to the University. This is to ensure that optimal conditions for the student�s successful reintegra\
tion into the University can be established.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
427 0 obj
<</E(a. The Fit for Study Committee will review the student�s      application to resume studies after Leave of Absence. b. The Fit for Study Committee will consider the student�s       support needs and, offer recommendations for         reducing barriers to \
reintegration and for enhancing       academic progress, and facilitate the student�s access       to these support mechanisms where possible.)/K[3]/Pg 30 0 R/S/H2/T(a. The Fit for Study Committee will review the student�s      application to resume studies after Leave of Absence. b. The Fit for Study Committee will consider the student�s       support needs and, offer recommendations for         reducing barriers to \
reintegration and for enhancing       academic progress, and facilitate the student�s access       to these support mechanisms where possible.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
428 0 obj
<</E(The University has the amanah to protect the health and safety of all students. In cases where there is a substantial risk of harm to others resulting from the student�s mental health difficulty, and adequate supports cannot reasonably be established, the\
 Fit for Study Committee may recommend to the Senate not to grant re-admission.)/K[4]/Pg 30 0 R/S/H2/T(The University has the amanah to protect the health and safety of all students. In cases where there is a substantial risk of harm to others resulting from the student�s mental health difficulty, and adequate supports cannot reasonably be established, the\
 Fit for Study Committee may recommend to the Senate not to grant re-admission.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
